# visual census: the constraints the ratified corpus EXHIBITS — derived, never typed;
# regenerate via `cargo run -p layout-probe --example freeze` and ratify the diff.
#
# Every row is freeze-stable: a floor or a maximum a new corpus member moves VISIBLY.
# A derived floor is DESCRIPTIVE of the corpus; committing this file is the normative
# act — from then on erosion is a red gate naming the movement, and raising a
# standard by example is a reviewable diff too.

corpus: 6 diagrams (the source grid, rendered by the stable engine)
horizontal floor (smallest within-rank gap): 4
vertical floor (smallest rank gap): 2
widest rank: 2 nodes
rank alignment: every rank shares one row (no overlaps)

# locality witness — insertion displacement, MEASURED (computed by the real
# engines, never asserted): max |Δ| of pre-existing nodes when one node joins.
# The early-sorting name exposes the stable engine's name/position coupling;
# the late-sorting name is the benign case. Another face of the one tradeoff.
insert `_new` (sorts early): stable moves 4, eager moves 0
insert `zz` (sorts late):   stable moves 0, eager moves 0
